  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "o3",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "The site and its sitemap",
      "excerpt": "The site and its sitemap",
      "text": "actually, I think the site references the pages, so e.g. the page names can be translated or moved",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T17:42:56.683Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:23.305Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  the site file now holds each page's address, name and parameters, and a page file holds only what it shows and does.  So a page moves or gets a translated name without changing the page;  links name the page and the site makes the address (Overview 1.3, marked).</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:09.577Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "o5",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "A page: its jobs, then its mockup",
      "excerpt": "A page: its jobs, then its mockup",
      "text": "the jobs bit should persist.  Should optionall express of the \"jobs\" as Agile Stories",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T17:44:03.680Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:24.211Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  a page's jobs are saved with it for good, into the real site, and each may be written as an Agile story (\"As a ..., I want ..., so that ...\"), with its \"done when\" checks under it (Overview 1.5, marked).  It becomes its own phase, Page Jobs.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:10.312Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "p-site-file#field-3",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Site File",
      "excerpt": "The sitemap is a Spell file the language reads : a link to a page that's gone, o",
      "text": "Let's use the star wars site as an example as well as spellUI",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T21:53:50.597Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "The example site is Spell UI's",
      "offset": 576,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T21:54:48.689Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:03:04.964Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P1's plan:  a second example site from the start, a small Star Wars site (films, people, planets, a <code>:film</code> and a <code>:person</code> page, a settings dialog, a person sidebar), beside Spell UI's.  The click-through phase builds its mockups on it.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c4": {
      "anchor": "p-site-file#field-5",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Site File",
      "excerpt": "A site is a built-in TEMPLATE written in Spell, beside the notebook's (Notebook.",
      "text": "has an analysis page",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T21:55:08.892Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "has an analysis",
      "offset": 777,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:03:05.818Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P1's plan:  the site lists its parts the way any thing's are written, <code>- it has an analysis page at \"/analyses/:analysis\"</code>, one line each.  The page itself still says <code>- it has an analysis</code>, which is where the parameter's type comes from.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c5": {
      "anchor": "p-site-file#field-5",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Site File",
      "excerpt": "A site is a built-in TEMPLATE written in Spell, beside the notebook's (Notebook.",
      "text": "also e.g. `it has a settings dialog` and `it has a syntax sidebar`",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T21:55:32.758Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "site file names",
      "offset": 803,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T21:55:55.318Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:03:06.513Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P1's plan:  a site holds DIALOGS and SIDEBARS beside its pages, <code>it has a settings dialog</code>, <code>it has a syntax sidebar</code>:  named once, opened from any page, no address of their own;  drawn as <code>&lt;ui-modal&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;ui-flyout&gt;</code>.  P2 opens them with <code>show the settings dialog</code>.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c6": {
      "anchor": "p-pages-by-address#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Pages By Address",
      "excerpt": "Open the example site in Run: its first page shows; change the address to /butto",
      "text": "ALSO `show the analysis page with this analysis`",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T21:56:49.783Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "go to",
      "offset": 192,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T21:57:03.060Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:03:07.190Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P2's plan:  <code>show the analysis page with this analysis</code> works beside <code>go to ...</code>, and <code>show the settings dialog</code> / <code>show the syntax sidebar</code> open the site's dialogs and sidebars.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c7": {
      "anchor": "p-pages-by-address#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Pages By Address",
      "excerpt": "Open the example site in Run: its first page shows; change the address to /butto",
      "text": "\"no such page.  Would you like to create one?\"",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T21:57:38.974Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "no such page\" page",
      "offset": 450,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T21:57:39.687Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:03:07.885Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P2's plan:  \"No such page.  Would you like to create one?\"  While designing, its button adds the page to the site file at that address and makes its empty page file, one undo step;  a visitor of a published site sees only \"No such page\".</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c8": {
      "anchor": "p-site-file#field-5",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Site File",
      "excerpt": "A site is a built-in TEMPLATE written in Spell, beside the notebook's (Notebook.",
      "text": "e.g. `spell ui is a site in the cloud` or `...at user@folder` etc",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T21:58:31.127Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "spell ui is a site",
      "offset": 0,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T21:58:52.113Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:03:08.569Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P1's plan:  the site says where it lives, the way a place does:  <code>spell ui is a site at owen@spell/spell-ui</code>, or <code>... is a site in the cloud</code>, its first line on the place-creating rule.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c9": {
      "anchor": "p-editable-table#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Editable Table",
      "excerpt": "Click or arrow to a cell, type to replace it, Enter or Tab to move on, Escape to",
      "text": "Should feel like a spreadsheet, e.g. no rounded borders or padding around the field in this mode",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T22:07:18.187Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Each cell is edited by its field's",
      "offset": 95,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T22:07:36.600Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:14:23.117Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P8's plan:  while editable, the table looks like a spreadsheet:  square cells on a hairline grid, no rounded borders or padding around the field, the edited cell outlined with its editor filling it edge to edge, in every theme.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c10": {
      "anchor": "p-ui-diagram#field-4",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "UI Diagram",
      "excerpt": "Share first: the tree diagram's box measuring (TreeMeasure ) and its line drawin",
      "text": "generic `resizable` property on (most?) ui elements to turn on the resizing.  Constraints,\nmaybe `resizable=\"horizontally\" max-width=\"50%\"`",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T22:08:23.363Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Share first: the tree",
      "offset": 0,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T22:09:18.885Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:14:23.968Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P9's plan:  <code>resizable</code> becomes a generic attribute (<code>resizable</code>, <code>resizable=\"horizontally\"</code> or <code>\"vertically\"</code>), limited by the platform's own <code>max-width=\"50%\"</code>, <code>min-height</code> ..., a handle built once on the element base, sizes remembered for elements with an id.  First on <code>&lt;ui-diagram-node&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;ui-card&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;ui-segment&gt;</code>.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c11": {
      "anchor": "p-signed-in-ingest#field-4",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Signed-In Ingest",
      "excerpt": "Signing in: spell place sign-in <place> opens Spell's OWN sign-in window, throug",
      "text": "Screenshot mode: you size a browser to a particular size, I'll navigate to a page and type in the screenshot name and/or what to link it to",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T22:10:10.783Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Rows off pages: BrowserPage",
      "offset": 593,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T22:10:51.516Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:14:24.712Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P11's plan:  a screenshot mode, <code>spell site screenshots &lt;site&gt; --size 1440x900</code>:  a visible signed-in browser at that size, you go to a page, a small bar takes a name and/or the site page to link it to, and Save writes the picture into the private site repo and points that page at it.</p>"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
